      "correct": "3",
      "solution": "__Shortcut Trick__\n\nApply the V-BODMAS rule to solve the expression step-by-step from inside to outside:\n\nVinculum (Bar): 16 − 10 = 6\n\nRound Brackets: 12 − 6 = 6\n\nCurly & Square Brackets: 14 − 6 = 8 → 12 − 8 = 4\n\nFinal Subtraction: 20 − 4 = 16\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 16.**\n\n**__Alternate Method__**\n\n**Given:**\n\nExpression = 20 − [12 − {14 − (12 − 16 − 10)}]\n\n**Concept Used:**\n\nV-BODMAS Rule (Vinculum, Brackets, Of, Division, Multiplication, Addition, Subtraction)\n\nOrder of solving brackets: Bar → () → {} → []\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 20 − [12 − {14 − (12 − 16 − 10)}]\n\n⇒ 20 − [12 − {14 − (12 − 6)}]\n\n⇒ 20 − [12 − {14 − 6}]\n\n⇒ 20 − [12 − 8]\n\n⇒ 20 − 4\n\n⇒ 16\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 16.**\n\n**__Additional Information__**\n\nV-BODMAS Rule\n\nV stands for Vinculum or Bar bracket. It acts as an overarching group. Even if operations like subtraction and multiplication are present under it, they are strictly resolved first.\n\nOrder of Brackets\n\nEvaluate nested brackets in the exact order: Vinculum (Bar) → Parentheses () → Braces {} → Square Brackets [].\n\nSigns in Simplification\n\nWhen a negative sign precedes a bracket, the sign of each term inside the bracket mathematically flips when the bracket is removed or resolved.\n</p",
